)$ shown above. The Fourier series of the $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼-1+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{12}{\\pi (2n-1)}sin\\,((2n-1)x).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nAt $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nsin\\,((2n-1)\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2}))={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is \n{{field-2}}\nat $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{2n-1}={{field-4}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite our Fourier series as\n\n$$\nf(x)∼-1+\\frac{12}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2n-1}\\cdot sin\\,((2n-1)x).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that at $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nsin\\,((2n-1)\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2}))=sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-n\\pi )=(-1)^{n}.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is $\\text{continuous}$ at $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=-4.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =-1+\\frac{12}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2n-1}\\cdot sin\\,((2n-1)\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\ -4 & =-1+\\frac{12}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2n-1}\\cdot (-1)^{n} \\\\ -3 & =\\frac{12}{\\pi }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{2n-1} \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{2n-1} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{2n-1} & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402338 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34e78128-47e4-5867-8d9d-3e3880cad539" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402340} {:answer/id #uuid "98c90103-4a5a-5ee2-9a58-bde0723208bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 1759